Z||000000||fieroburton||08-06-2001||08:43 PM||||can you make Indy air scoops function like a ram air scoop by directing it to the air intake ?<BR> if so how ?<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    [img]www.geocities.com/fieroburton/25_25.jpg[/img]<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||08-06-2001||08:49 PM||||By running duct work to the air intake on a V-6, usually using a cone shaped K&N air filter inside the scoop. On a 4-cyl, you just need to make a "ram air" air filter housing like the old muscle cars. (open top with a foam gasket to seal the housing to the decklid.) The 4-cyl's are very easy to do since the air filter is near the center where the scoop goes.<BR>I was (and might still) run it to the intake but I like how well it keeps my engine compartment very cool. I may try and split the scoop so 1/2 goes to the intake and the other 1/2 cools the engine compartment. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||08-06-2001||10:33 PM||||an '84 air filter housing is a little different than my '87 one, i don't know if it would be worth changing valve cover and filter housing (and what ever else would be needed) but on mine i just cut the filter housing snorkle off at a point close to just beneath the scoop. then i used some 3" pipe and welded it to the new opening so it sticks up just under the scoop, kind of offset on the snorkle. it's pretty ugly.uglier still when the scoops off. there a 3" pipe sticking a couple inches out of the lid. i just did it 'cause i had the scoop on and i wanted to be able to say it was funtional. hopefully if the engine change ever happens i'll work out something better. actually it would probaly be easier to do with the '84 snorkle 'cause it runs right down the middle under the lid, but i think you would lose the heat riser funtion of it. it also seems like it would be harmful in a big rain but being caught in a few pretty good storms hasn't seemed to affect it.<P>if there's more people interested in them let me mention again trying a group purchase from someone who makes them, if someone can swing the deal.||||reg||1
